        "translations": [
          {
            "lang": "en-US",
            "name": "Xī Hú Lóngjǐng",
            "transcription": "Xīhú lóngjǐng",
            "description": "**Imperial green tea from West Lake: flat leaf, orchid and roasted chestnut aroma, sweet aftertaste.**\n\nXi Hu Long Jing (West Lake Dragon Well) is the most famous Chinese green tea, topping the list of 'China's Ten Famous Teas'. It is produced exclusively by hand in the vicinity of Hangzhou's West Lake from select buds and one to two leaves. It has a characteristic flat shape, a delicate bean-floral aroma, and a deep flavor with a bright umami note.\n\n**Tasting note:** Delicate, smooth infusion with expressive umami, notes of roasted chestnut, floral sweetness, and a long refreshing finish.\n\n## Brewing recipes\n- **gongfu:** 80°C, 5 g / 100 ml, 10s, 3 steeps\n- **western:** 75°C, 3 g / 200 ml, 180s, 2 steeps",
            "seo": "xihu-longjing",
            "metaTitle": "Xi Hu Long Jing: Description, History, and Taste of the Legendary Tea",
            "metaDescription": "Xi Hu Long Jing — imperial green tea from Hangzhou. Learn all about the taste, aroma, legends, and proper brewing of the West Lake Dragon Well."
          },
          {
            "lang": "ru-RU",
            "name": "Си Ху Лун Цзин",
